    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309-a1">

                <pb facs="0796" n="1426" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1426"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>Every individual born in Belgium of a foreigner may, during the year which
                    follows the epoch of his majority, reclaim the quality of a Belgian, provided
                    that, in case he shall reside in Belgium, he declare that it is his intention to
                    fix his domicile there, and in ease he shall reside in a foreign country he
                    makes his submission to fix his domicile in Belgium, and establish himself there
                    within one year, from the date of the act of submission. (Article 9, civil
                    code.)</p>
                <p>The person born in Belgium of alien parents residing there, who shall have
                    neglected to make the declaration prescribed by the ninth article of the civil
                    code, may, if he is an inhabitant of the country, ask for full naturalization
                    without being required to show that he has rendered eminent services to the
                    state. (Law of September 27, 1835, article 2.)</p>
            </div>
